  {
    "ID": 45,
    "Personaggio/soggetto": "Toys in the antique store",
    "Film/corto": "Toy Story 4",
    "Anno": 2019,
    "Regista/autore": "Josh Cooley",
    "Trama": "Woody has always been confident about his place in the world..and that his priority is taking care of his kid, whether that’s Andy or Bonnie. But when Bonnie adds a reluctant new toy called “Forky” to her room, a road trip adventure alongside old and new friends will show Woody how big the world can be for a toy.",
    "Link 1": "Trailer: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wmiIUN-7qhE",
    "Link 2": null,
    "Link 3": null,
    "Categoria Innovazione (tag) 1": "Motion / Background",
    "Nome Innovazione 1": "Motion Capture ",
    "Paragrafo motivazione innovazione 1": "there were over 10,000 antiques in this store, and Pixar had to find a way to program each and every one with varying levels of wear and tear.",
    "Info specifiche sul funzionamento 1": "Animators tackled this challenge by assigning three different ages to the antiques: fairly new, moderately aged, and extremely aged. The computer than gave the items surface details that fit those ages, from micro-scratches on china platters to wear and tear on old rugs.",
    "Categoria Innovazione (tag) 2": null,
    "Nome Innovazione 2": null,
    "Paragrafo Funzionamento generale 2": null,
    "Funzionamento - info maggiori su tecnologie 2": null,
    "Copertina": "assets/images/personaggi/45/copertina_45",
