  {
    "ID": 54,
    "Personaggio/soggetto": "Anxiety",
    "Film/corto": "Inside Out 2",
    "Anno": 2024,
    "Regista/autore": "Kelsey Mann",
    "Trama": "“Inside Out 2” returns to the mind of newly minted teenager Riley just as headquarters is undergoing a sudden demolition to make room for something entirely unexpected: new Emotions! Joy, Sadness, Anger, Fear and Disgust, who’ve long been running a successful operation by all accounts, aren’t sure how to feel when Anxiety shows up. And it looks like she’s not alone.",
    "Link 1": "Trailer: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LEjhY15eCx0",
    "Link 2": null,
    "Link 3": null,
    "Categoria Innovazione (tag) 1": "Modeling",
    "Nome Innovazione 1": "Curvenet and Profile Mover",
    "Paragrafo motivazione innovazione 1": "to create reusable hand rig",
    "Info specifiche sul funzionamento 1": "these tools were used to create, for the first time at Pixar, a fully articulated Hand Curvenet as a shareable rig.\nThe result was fully rigged hands for all of our characters, out-of-the-box, without doing any rigging work on the geometry, regardless of shape or topology. ",
    "Categoria Innovazione (tag) 2": "Modeling",
    "Nome Innovazione 2": "Mouth Corner Rig",
    "Paragrafo Funzionamento generale 2": "Anxiety is a character that requires specialized mouth rigging configurations for flexible and precise animation control. It requires both rough adjustments and finer details to create a wide array of facial expressions.",
    "Funzionamento - info maggiori su tecnologie 2": "the team devised a mouth corner rig consisting\nof three layers of controls. The first manipulates the outer silhouette of the mouth\nand face, allowing for broad adjustments to shape and expression. The second\nfocuses on moving the mouth corners within the face silhouette, and the third is\ndedicated to refining the outer silhouette without affecting the teeth placement.",
